    "sources": [
      {
        "title": "Bad news for Trump ahead of the midterms: it’s still the economy, stupid",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/15/trump-economy-midterm-elections",
        "publisher": "Guardian",
        "category": "Elections",
        "published_at": "2026-10-15T12:00:12Z",
        "primary": false
      },
      {
        "title": "Key US voters say economy is getting worse ahead of midterms, exclusive poll finds",
        "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/15/voters-economy-cost-of-living-prices-poll",
        "publisher": "Guardian",
        "category": "U.S.",
        "published_at": "2026-10-15T09:00:13Z",
        "primary": false,
        "excerpt": "Nearly 61% believe country is in recession and 65% of independents say economy is worse, according to new Harris pollOur reporters answer your questions about the US economy and the midterm electionsWhat is your personal ‘recession indicator’?With the midterm elections less than three weeks away, key voting groups including independents, rural voters and even some Republicans are increasingly disenchanted with Donald Trump’s economy, according to an exclusive Harris poll for the Guardian.The majority of those surveyed were pessimistic about the economy, with three-quarters of Americans saying ",
        "ai_editor": {
          "id": "c6c972789af116444f82",
          "priority": 3,
          "section": "brief",
          "major": false,
          "context": "The Harris poll reports that 65% of independents believe the economy is worsening. Conducted online among 3,998 US adults, it measures economic perceptions, not election outcomes; the supplied article gives no margin of error.",
